In article <26843d50.283b@petunia.CalPoly.EDU> games@polyslo.CalPoly.EDU (Fun and Games) writes:
   I am attempting to code the shopping mall as was discussed. Can anyone
   point me out to some information on lev_comp and how to properly interface
   it to the game code?

Building the actual level isn't hard to do with the level compiler, 
neither is modifying the code to use your level (I have done both for
a shopping mall level back when it was first discussed).  The sticky
point was that while yo can put a shopkeeper in a room, you cannot
make a room into a shop.  Shops are special rooms, built separately
from ordinary rooms, and the special level compiler doesn't know how to
make shops.

You can modify the level compiler to make shops (the hooks to do so are 
in the code already) or you can build the shopping mall level from scratch.
Neither is easy however.

Best of luck, I am not sure if I still have my code siting around, but
if you get stuck, sen me a note.

